<title>TURKEY: TURKEY SETS 13-MONTH BOND AUCTION FOR TUESDAY.</title>
<headline>TURKEY SETS 13-MONTH BOND AUCTION FOR TUESDAY.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish central bank said the Treasury would auction on Tuesday 13-month (399-day) bonds after it sold 217.4 trillion lira of 399-day bonds on March 18 at 106.77 percent yields, including witholding tax.</p>
<p>    Maturity    : April 29, 1998</p>
<p>    Amount	: -</p>
<p>    Coupon	: -</p>
<p>    Auction date: March 25, 1997</p>
<p>    Value date  : March 26, 1997</p>
<p>The Treasury has 189.3 trillion lira of domestic debt repayments due on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
</text>
